course: dictionary
lesson: 6457
title: Narrow: not wide, and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Narrow means not wide. There is only a small distance from one side to the other. «Walk in single file, because the path is narrow and there is little room for two.» The word tells you the space is small.
explain: Narrow can also mean only just. A narrow win is won by a small margin, and a narrow escape is a close call. The words around it give the clue: a path is about width, but an escape is about how near something came to going wrong.
explain: Narrow can be a verb too. To narrow is to become less wide, and to narrow something down is to make a list of choices smaller. When you narrow down answers in a puzzle, you cross out the ones that cannot be right.
fact: «Narrow» means not wide, with only a small distance from one side to the other.
fact: «A narrow escape» means a close call, when something only just does not go wrong.
fact: «Narrow it down» means make a list of choices smaller, by ruling out answers.
fact: «Narrow-minded» means not willing to accept new or different ideas.
fact: Narrow can be an adjective (narrower, narrowest) or a verb (narrows, narrowed, narrowing).
exercise: «The path was narrow, so the children walked in single file.» What does narrow mean here? | Quick and easy | Very long and tall | *Not wide, with little space from side to side | Very dark and cold
exercise: «They had a narrow escape from the wave.» What does narrow escape mean? | A quiet walk on the sand | A long holiday by the sea | A wide, safe beach | *A close call, only just getting away
exercise: Ben has three pet choices and wants to narrow it down. What is one way to do that? | Choose all three | Ask nobody and wait | *Cross out the choices that cannot be right, until fewer are left | Pick the biggest choice without thinking
test: Nadia says narrow-minded means small. What does it really mean? | *Not willing to accept new or different ideas | Happy with everything | Quick to change its mind | Very thin and tall
test: «The river began to narrow as it reached the rocks.» What does narrow mean here? | To shine brightly | To stop flowing for ever | *To become less wide | To become wider and deeper
exam: «Dogs' canines make deep narrow holes that trap germs.» What does narrow tell you about the holes? | They are shiny and smooth | They are full of water | *They are not wide, with only a small width | They are very wide and open
